[size=6][b]Ysmir — A Lore-Friendly Shout Overhaul[/b][/size]
[i]The Dragonborn's power should be expressed through the Voice.[/i]

Ysmir reworks all 27 player shouts from Skyrim, Dawnguard and Dragonborn. Shout more often, let the dragon souls you carry strengthen your Voice, and use newly read Words of Power immediately.

An ESL-flagged ESP with native Papyrus and included visual assets. No SKSE, DLL, MCM or additional mod masters.

[size=5][b]The Dragonborn's Voice[/b][/size]

[b]Five-second base recovery at every word level.[/b] All 27 shouts use 5 / 5 / 5 seconds. Have you ever wondered why the Greybeards and Miraak can shout so frequently? Their shout cooldowns are 5 / 5 / 5 seconds, providing a reference for a lore-accurate shout cooldown. Now all of the Dragonborn's shouts use 5 / 5 / 5 seconds—even shouts added by other mods. This is the chosen baseline for a master of the Voice.

[b]Dragon souls strengthen your shouts.[/b] Every dragon soul you currently hold adds 2.5% to eligible magnitude and duration. According to the lore, the Dragonborn absorbs dragon souls and the dragons' understanding. Miraak steals your dragon souls to strengthen himself, and Kaalgrontiid even sought to absorb the power of his fellow dragons to become a new moon and challenge Akatosh. Now every dragon soul increases the power and duration of your shouts by 2.5%.

[b]Read a Word Wall and use its word.[/b] Newly read words unlock without spending a dragon soul. If absorbing a dragon soul already gives you its knowledge, why do you need to spend a soul to learn a new word? It sounds like having to consume a spell tome when you learn magic from it (laughs).

Ysmir treats the Dragonborn's innate affinity for the dragon language as immediate practical understanding. This deliberately changes vanilla's word-unlocking mechanic; it does not claim that ordinary mortals learn the Voice this way. Previously learned but locked words keep their normal unlock route, and quest-taught words follow their quests.

[b]Nearly all shout effects now carry the MagicShout keyword.[/b] This fits the lore and lets the dragon-soul scaling system automatically strengthen effects tagged with MagicShout. Shout effects added by other mods benefit too if they carry the MagicShout keyword.

[size=5][b]The shouts[/b][/size]

Values below are base values before soul bonuses. Every shout also receives the five-second base cooldown. Where an effect already serves its purpose, Ysmir keeps that role and makes it grow with the Dragonborn.

[size=4][b]Skyrim[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Animal Allegiance:[/b] Animals now remain loyal to you for longer as your dragon soul count increases.
[*][b]Aura Whisper:[/b] Detection uses separate ranges for friendly and hostile auras, with a 10 / 20 / 30-second base duration. Keeps its scouting role while soul growth extends useful awareness.
[*][b]Become Ethereal:[/b] Preserves ethereal protection and its 8 / 13 / 18-second baseline; souls extend the window. Keeps it a tool for movement and survival, with meditation improving recovery.
[*][b]Call Dragon:[/b] Keeps the full three-word call to Odahviing, with five-second recovery. Calling an ally should not lock out the rest of the Voice for five minutes.
[*][b]Call of Valor:[/b] The three heroes and their related variants are level 150, with a 60-second base summon duration. Heroes who fought Alduin should remain useful beside a powerful Dragonborn.
[*][b]Clear Skies:[/b] Retains its weather-clearing behavior and 25 / 40 / 60-second baseline. Faster recovery makes repeated environmental use less cumbersome.
[*][b]Disarm:[/b] Retains disarming and the 12 / 20 / 30 base level caps; eligible strength grows with souls. Lets the shout remain useful as enemies become stronger.
[*][b]Dismay:[/b] Keeps fear, removes the separate push and broadens the third word's eligible targets. Gives it a clear crowd-control identity distinct from Unrelenting Force.
[*][b]Dragonrend:[/b] Keeps grounding, dragon restrictions and quest behavior, with a 15 / 18 / 22-second base duration. Improves repeat use without changing its story purpose.
[*][b]Elemental Fury:[/b] Why does Elemental Fury have no elements? That makes no sense. Now direct 1.3× / 1.5× / 1.7× attack speed works with enchanted weapons. Attacks can independently trigger fire, frost and shock bursts, each with a 50% chance and a two-second interval per element.
[*][b]Fire Breath:[/b] Retains 50 / 70 / 90 base damage, burning and stagger; eligible damage grows with souls. The Dragonborn's breath grows with their acquired power. Because Fire Breath deals 90 damage over one second, and dragon souls also extend its duration, total damage actually scales with the square of the multiplier.
[*][b]Frost Breath:[/b] Retains 10 / 14 / 18 damage per second for five seconds, slow and stagger. The Black Book upgrade adds damage and frost wyrms from eligible kills, giving it a distinct progression path. At three words, Frost Breath deals 18 damage per second for five seconds, totaling 90 damage. Since dragon souls also extend its duration, total damage actually scales with the square of the multiplier.
[*][b]Ice Form:[/b] Retains encasement, break-on-hit behavior and a 15 / 30 / 60-second baseline. Eligible damage and duration grow, keeping it a disabling shout rather than simply another breath attack.
[*][b]Kyne's Peace:[/b] Why does the voice of Kynareth affect only animals? That makes no sense at all. The range of eligible targets now extends beyond animals, and the third word reaches more target types. Gives a peaceful use of the Voice a broader role.
[*][b]Marked for Death:[/b] Causes temporary armor loss and adds 25% magic weakness for 10 / 20 / 30 seconds. Creates a debuff window for follow-up physical and magical attacks.
[*][b]Slow Time:[/b] Why does a shout that commands time to slow also slow your own time? You can simply command time not to slow for you. Now the world moves at 30% / 20% / 10% speed while you move normally. Souls extend its 8 / 12 / 16-second duration.
[*][b]Storm Call:[/b] Alduin can summon meteors with a range of 600, while your storm has a mere 150? All ranks now use an initial target-acquisition range of 600, matching the 600 area in Alduin's combat meteor-storm spell. Retains outdoor weather and random native lightning, with 40 / 60 / 80 base Health damage and, like other shock spells, half as much Magicka damage. Since the lightning effects are tagged with MagicShout, Mora's wonderful power that keeps your shouts and spells from harming companions now applies to Storm Call too. After you obtain Companion's Insight from a Black Book, it prevents Storm Call from damaging companions who meet its native protection conditions; lightning can still target them.
[*][b]Throw Voice:[/b] All word levels recover in five seconds, matching the original third word. Makes the distraction tool more convenient without changing its purpose.
[*][b]Unrelenting Force:[/b] If your Voice keeps growing stronger, then logically it should send enemies flying farther and farther, right? Now the more dragon souls you have, the farther enemies are thrown. The Black Book reward emphasizes added damage rather than disintegration. The Voice's physical force grows with its wielder.
[*][b]Whirlwind Sprint:[/b] You can turn yourself into a missile with a single word, yet enemies block you with their bodies like a wall? That makes no sense either. Now Whirlwind Sprint staggers enemies along your path.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Dawnguard[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Drain Vitality:[/b] It is called “Drain Vitality,” yet it only damages the enemy? Now the Health, Magicka and Stamina lost by enemies are all drained into you.
[*][b]Soul Tear:[/b] Have you ever wondered why dragons in ESO use Soul Tear as a large-area AoE, while all you can do is throw a rock that hits the first enemy? Now Soul Tear's projectile pierces every enemy, dealing damage, trapping souls and reanimating enemies all along its path.
[*][b]Summon Durnehviir:[/b] Preserves the full shout and 180-second native summon baseline, with shorter recovery and duration growth. Keeps your ally available without locking you out of other shouts for five minutes.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Dragonborn[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Battle Fury:[/b] Extends the ally buff to eligible commanded actors while retaining 1.3× / 1.5× / 1.7× speed and a 60 / 120 / 180-second base duration. Lets the Voice support the allies you actually fight beside.
[*][b]Bend Will:[/b] The first word can command eligible targets up to base level 30 for ten seconds. Later words retain broader control and the third word's dragon-taming role. Gives the first word a practical use without removing the quest restrictions.
[*][b]Cyclone:[/b] Retains the damaging whirlwind and 50 / 75 / 100 base damage, with eligible soul growth. Makes an existing crowd-control shout available as part of regular combat.
[*][b]Dragon Aspect:[/b] Removes the daily limit; adds Destruction and Restoration strength, replaces elemental resistance with general Magic Resistance, and retains the third word's cooldown benefit and Ancient Dragonborn support. Treats the aspect as an expression of your dragon nature, rather than a once-daily resource.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Meditation and rewards[/b][/size]

Fus meditation retains stagger benefits and adds protection from being thrown. Feim improves Health, Magicka and Stamina regeneration while ethereal. Yol retains its Fire Breath bonus. The High Hrothgar pilgrimage blessing adds 25% to eligible shout effects. Black Book rewards remain meaningful upgrades to Force, Flame and Frost.

[size=5][b]Installation and compatibility[/b][/size]

Install with Vortex or MO2 and enable [b]Ysmir - Shout System Overhaul.esp[/b]. The runtime masters are Skyrim, Update, Dawnguard and Dragonborn. All required custom resources are included.

Other shout overhauls can edit the same records. Load order determines the winning behavior, so combine them with a carefully made patch.

[size=5][b]Credits and disclosure[/b][/size]

Inspired by [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/36276]Forceful Tongue[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/93681]Elemental Fury and Battle Fury overhaul[/url], and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/49359]Whirlwind Sprint Redone[/url]. The code was reworked with the simplest, most native approach. This mod contains just 12 scripts, all using native effects already present in the game.

